所以，哦，对我来说很大一部分原因是《抑制热情》这部剧。

318
00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:40.980
And of course in Curb, you're improvising off, um, you know, an outline less than you
当然在《抑制热情》里，你是基于，嗯，你知道，一个大纲进行即兴表演，比你们

319
00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:46.080
guys had a great deal less, I would say, but you guys still had room to improvise.
用的少得多，我想是这样，但你们依然有即兴发挥的空间。

320
00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:46.320
Right.
没错。

321
00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:50.200
So I knew, oh, there's going to be, this is like Curb.
所以我知道，哦，这会是，这就像《抑制热情》一样。

322
00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.760
And I had had such a good time on Curb.
而且我在《抑制热情》里过得非常愉快。

323
00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.860
It was doing that show.
就是拍那部剧的时候。

324
00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:59.120
I was like, oh my God, this is the best thing you can get in show business.
我当时想，天哪，这是演艺圈里你能得到的最棒的事情了。

325
00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:05.120
If you can get this to happen, a show with an ensemble of people that you like and that
如果你能促成这件事，和一群你喜欢的人组成剧组，他们

326
00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:11.720
are funny and that you get room to just invent and just goof around, this is the beSt.
既风趣，你又有空间去创造和胡闹，这真是太棒了。

327
00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:18.200
So I was excited to do the auditions for the office because I knew it had that dimension.
所以我很兴奋能参加《办公室》的试镜，因为我知道它有那个维度。

328
00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:24.120
And look, when I did the Ben Stiller show, I walked away from that going, I got to create
你看，当我拍《本·斯蒂勒秀》时，我离开时心想，我得再和朋友们

329
00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:26.060
a show again with my friends.
创作一部剧。

330
00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:26.960
Yeah.
是的。

331
00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:31.580
Waking up in the morning and picking up Andy Dick and picking up Ginny Garofalo and driving
早上醒来，接上安迪·迪克和吉妮·加罗法洛，开车

332
00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:38.780
out to wherever the hell we had some cheap ass set or we're stealing locations and goofing
去往我们那廉价的片场，或者去偷拍外景，整天

333
00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:42.700
around all day long and laughing is the greatest, you know?
胡闹、大笑，真是太棒了，你懂吗？

334
00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:47.000
So when that show ended, I was like, I have to recreate that.
所以当那部剧结束时，我就想，我必须重现那种感觉。

335
00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:50.540
And so when I finished Curb, I was like, I have to recreate that.
所以当我拍完《抑制热情》时，我就想，我必须重现那种感觉。

336
00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.020
But I still haven't.
但我至今还没做到。

337
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.540
Are you still working on it?
你还在努力吗？

338
00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.820
Not really.
算不上吧。

339
00:14:56.180 --> 00:15:03.020
This weird thing happened where I got into a drama and it's a lot of work and you don't
发生了一件奇怪的事，我开始演正剧了，那工作量很大，而且你根本

340
00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.300
improvise at all.
没法即兴发挥。

341
00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:10.620
And then I got into action movies, which again, you don't, you know, it's, you can, you know,
然后我开始拍动作片，同样，你不能，你知道，这，你可以，你知道，

342
00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:16.140
obviously like any movie, but even maybe more, maybe it's more malleable than a lot of
显然像任何电影一样，但甚至可能更多，也许它比很多

343
00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:20.080
films, you know, you can work with the moment and invent.
电影更具可塑性，你知道，你可以利用当下进行创造。

344
00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.260
And that is especially true of the fight sequences.
在打斗场面中尤其如此。

345
00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:24.280
Really?
真的吗？

346
00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:24.800
Interesting.
有意思。

347
00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:25.200
Yes.
是的。

348
00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:26.660
Wait, they're not just like.
等等，它们不是那种……

349
00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:27.780
They are choreographed.
它们是编排好的。

350
00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.700
They're absolutely choreographed and rehearsed.
它们绝对是经过编排和排练的。

351
00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:35.980
But when you get on set and it's time to do it and you see a shot you didn't have, you
但当你到了片场，真正开始拍摄时，你发现了一个之前没想到的镜头，你

352
00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:43.640
see a move that you didn't think of, the set isn't quite built the way the layout was and
看到了一个没想到的动作，片场搭建得和设计图不太一样，

353
00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:49.800
something goes wrong or looks better and you go, no, no, no, no, no, don't hit me.
或者出了点岔子，又或者效果更好，于是你说，不不不，别打我。

354
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:50.640
I'll hit him.
我来打他。

355
00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:54.280
If you fall over and I'll punch you in the face.
如果你摔倒了，我就往你脸上来一拳。

356
00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.940
And then everybody goes, ah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
然后大家都说，啊，对对对，就是这样。

357
00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:01.860
And then you do that thing and then you look at it on camera and you go, oh, that was awesome.
接着你照做了，再看回放时你会说，噢，太棒了。

358
00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.300
That looks so real.
看起来真真实。

359
00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:10.400
Well, I was very surprised to discover that aspect of doing that, of the inventiveness
我非常惊讶地发现了这种拍摄方式的另一面，那种创造力

360
00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:14.820
and teamwork that those sequences, I think, always take.
以及那些动作场面往往需要的团队协作。

361
00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.040
But I mean, every movie's different.
不过我是说，每部电影都不一样。

362
00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:23.200
But I'm going to keep those in my repertoire, I hope, if I make more action movies, which
但我希望如果我以后再拍动作片，我会把这些经验保留在我的技能库里，

363
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:24.200
it looks like I might.
看起来我可能会拍。

364
00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.600
Well, shocker, we have never done an action movie, Jenna and I.
噢，真令人震惊，我和珍娜从来没拍过动作片。

365
00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:28.260
Does that surprise you?
这让你感到惊讶吗？

366
00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:28.660
Does that surprise you?
这让你感到惊讶吗？

367
00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:29.360
That we are not.
我们没拍过。

368
00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.720
Well, doesn't it surprise you that I did be one?
难道我拍了一部动作片不让你感到惊讶吗？

369
00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:37.140
I mean, in a way, I remember when Naomi told me that you were going to do your first action
我是说，某种程度上，我记得娜奥米告诉我你要拍第一部动作片时，

370
00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.080
film and I was like, really?
我的反应是，真的吗？

371
00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:40.520
Really?
真的吗？

372
00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.520
Jenna, we shouldn't count ourselves out.
珍娜，我们不该妄自菲薄。

373
00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.700
Maybe we should out there for us.
也许我们该去争取一下。

374
00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:45.220
Absolutely.
绝对的。

375
00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.220
Mom Detectives.
《妈妈侦探》。

376
00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:47.780
Action.
动作片。

377
00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:49.540
That's our spinoff show.
那是我们的衍生剧。

378
00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.100
Detectives.
侦探。

379
00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.160
Yeah, Mom Detectives.
对，《妈妈侦探》。

380
00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.400
Just don't punch anything.
只是别打人就行。

381
00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:53.180
We do.
我们会打的。

382
00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:54.300
Mom Detectives do.
《妈妈侦探》会打的。

383
00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:56.840
Solving crimes no one cares about.
专门侦破没人关心的案件。

384
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.960
That's our log line.
这就是我们的宣传语。

385
00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:01.700
I did an improv pilot right before I got The Office.
我在接拍《办公室》之前做过一个即兴表演的试播集。

386
00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:02.300
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

387
00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.340
It was called Salon Royale.
叫《皇家沙龙》。

388
00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:08.820
And it was me and Ian Roberts and Betty Cahill and Dave Brzezowski.
主演是我、伊恩·罗伯茨、贝蒂·卡希尔和戴夫·布热佐夫斯基。

389
00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:09.220
Wow.
哇。

390
00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:11.660
And it was for the Oxygen Network.
那是为氧气频道拍的。

391
00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:15.580
It was the most fun I had had, like, ever on a job.
那是我工作以来最开心的一次经历。

392
00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.860
And I just knew it was going to go.
我当时就觉得它肯定能火。

393
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.480
It was just amazing.
真的太棒了。

394
00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:20.600
And then it didn't go.
结果没成。

395
00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.220
But if it had gone, I wouldn't have gotten The Office.
但如果成了，我就不会接拍《办公室》了。

396
00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.000
And I always think about that.
我经常会想到这一点。

397
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:33.080
But that kind of chemistry of having this loose outline and getting to improvise the beats of a scene with people who you truSt.
但那种化学反应，即拥有一个松散的大纲，并能与你信任的人即兴发挥出场景的节奏感，

398
00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.080
And it's so much fun.
真的太有趣了。

399
00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:35.920
Oh, it's the beSt.
噢，那是最棒的。

400
00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:36.460
Yeah.
是啊。

401
00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:43.920
I mean, I think acting in a drama that's really well written and intense and, you know, layered and all that.
我是说，我觉得参演一部剧本写得特别好、节奏紧凑、内涵丰富之类的作品，感觉很棒。

402
00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:49.240
But, you know, Better Call Saul, the star of the show is the writing, you know.
但你知道，《风骚律师》这部剧，真正的明星其实是它的剧本。

403
00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:56.900
And that has a great reward when you finish a scene and it's difficult and you feel that you connected with it, honestly.
当你完成一场高难度的戏，并且感觉自己真正融入其中时，那种成就感真的非常棒。

404
00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:03.180
But it's not as much fun as doing this, what we're talking about.
但那远不如我们现在聊的这种工作有趣。

405
00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:03.780
Yeah.
没错。

406
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:08.940
And, look, I would love, Jenna, I would love to find a show where I got to do this.
而且，听着，珍娜，我真的很想找到一部能让我做这种表演的剧。

407
00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.360
It really is the most fun.
这真的是最有趣的。

408
00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.760
Because I am a writer, too.
因为我也是个编剧。

409
00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:15.900
So, it lets you use that part of you or you're inventing things.
所以，这能让你发挥那方面的才能，或者说让你去创造一些东西。

410
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.380
And there's no question.
而且毫无疑问。

411
00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.760
You know, you do this thing and they say cut and you all laugh.
你知道，你演完这一段，导演喊停，然后大家都在笑。

412
00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.500
And that's just a good sign.
那绝对是个好兆头。

413
00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.320
It's the best time.
那是最好的时光。

414
00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.540
If you're laughing at work.
如果你在工作中能开怀大笑的话。

415
00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.000
We laughed every day.
我们每天都在笑。

416
00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.580
We did on the set of The Office.
我们在《办公室》剧组时就是这样。

417
00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.600
Like, every day there was a moment where you ruined a take because you were laughing.
几乎每天都有那么一刻，因为笑场而毁掉了一次拍摄。

418
00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.720
Bob, you mentioned that you are also a writer.
鲍勃，你提到过你也是一名编剧。

